      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were the \"department\" and \"businessUnit\" attributes. Merchant Services used \"businessUnit=merchant\" while Payments Ops used \"department=payments.\" This inconsistency caused the ingestion normalization process to fail to collapse these into a single canonical attribute, leading to Rules Engine matching failures.\n\nJin proposed a fast fix to add a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest that maps \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publishes a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change, can be hot-reloaded, is low risk, and does not require any changes to Okta flows or waiting on Okta change control. This approach allows immediate remediation without the 2\u20134 week delay needed for standardizing at the identity source (Okta) [art_79f625aafa16].",
