      "answer": "We have a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple accounts, not just MapleBridge. The customers exhibiting this pattern are City of Verdant Bay, Maple Regional Transit Authority, MapleBay Marketplace, MapleBridge Insurance, MapleFork Franchise Systems, MaplePath Career Institute, and MapleWest Bank.\n\nThe shared failure pattern in plain English is: After migrating from legacy workflow tooling to Orchestrator, approval workflows for Canada-specific policies fail because the rule evaluation precedence is incorrect. Specifically, global-default rules override or bypass region-specific (country or province) approval rules due to misordered rule evaluation priorities, schema key mismatches (such as 'country_code' versus 'country'), and delayed synchronization of schema registry versions across evaluation clusters. This results in approvals being stuck, auto-denied, routed incorrectly, or bypassed, which leads to manual overrides, escalations, and compliance risks. Immediate mitigations include deploying override rules to block automated approvals, routing approvals to manual approvers, enabling audit logs, and applying hotfixes to fix rule precedence evaluation. Evidence exports and audit trails are being generated for compliance verification.\n\nMapleBridge is not a one-off case; multiple customers across Canada show similar approval bypass or failure patterns post-migration, all linked to rule precedence and schema normalization issues [art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_54e35e2cb431, art_3db205cb21ca, art_e697b3abe158].",
